{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/j47cp4","slideIndex":8,"text":"The form requires name, email, phone, project type, location and message. Browser-native constraints validate required fields. A honeypot helps catch automated submissions. Frontend code posts JSON as text/plain and checks the returned success value. The supplied backend script creates a Google Form response, appends a Sheet row and sends an email. It then returns JSON. The configured deployed script has not been inspected or tested here, so storage and email delivery are not verified. The arrows summarize handling, not separate sequential APIs between each output. The success response returns from Apps Script to the browser.\n\nSources: src/components/contact/ContactForm.jsx; src/data.ts; google-apps-script-contact-submitter.gs"}
